Task: Document the template in this repo's own README

Summary:
Added a "Generating a new service from this template" section to the main
README: prerequisites (same as running the reference service, plus the same
GITHUB_ACTOR/GITHUB_TOKEN), the primary generation command (sbt new
file:///path/to/repo --domain_name=widget, pointed at the repo root), a
fallback using giter8's own giter8-launcher library directly for sbt versions
where the built-in `new` command doesn't resolve file:// URIs (documented
with the exact "Template not found for: file://..." symptom to watch for),
both template properties (domain_name, package) and their defaults/behavior,
post-generation steps (one sbt scalafmt pass expected), and the
naive-pluralization known limitation.

Files changed:
- README.md

Why: Completes this track's spec.md requirement that this repo document how
to actually use the template it ships.

Verification: ran both documented generation commands (the sbt new file://
form and the giter8-launcher fallback) against this exact repo from a clean
throwaway directory - both produced an identical, correct widget-service/
output pointed at the repo root (not src/main/g8), confirming the README's
exact commands are accurate and reproducible.
